+### Prebuilt agent CLIs
+
+By default the Claude Code agent installs itself in every trial container: it
+runs `apt-get` and downloads the native CLI from `downloads.claude.ai`, which
+is a full binary download per trial and fails on hosts that cannot reach that
+domain. When your evaluation image already ships the CLI, opt out of the
+per-trial install:
+
+```bash title="Verify the image's Claude Code instead of installing it"
+export SKILLEVALUATOR_DOCKER_PREBUILT_AGENTS=claude-code
+skillevaluator tier3 evaluate ./my-skill --agents claude-code --env-mode docker
+```
+
+Each trial then only runs `claude --version`; launch, credentials, and
+permission handling are unchanged. The image must provide `claude` on the agent
+user's `PATH` together with `ps` (`procps`), which Claude Code uses to clean up
+its process tree. Generated task images start `FROM python:3.12-slim`, and
+Docker uses a local image with that tag when one exists, so an operator-built
+image under that tag supplies the CLI to every generated task. If the image
+lacks the CLI, agent setup fails with exit 127 and an error naming this
+variable; add `--agent-runtime-preflight` to catch that in one bounded smoke
+trial before the full matrix runs.
+
+Only `claude-code` is supported, and only in `--env-mode docker`; other
+environment modes ignore the variable. Unsupported agent names, and providers
+whose compatibility wrapper installs the agent itself (such as `nv_build`),
+fail the run before any trial starts.
+
